{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 849ab1d5: the proposed R3a direction is accepted. Proceed to source edits.\n\n1. A key with no answer, or an unknown answer, is not kept and is not charged against the bound.\n2. A key takes a place only after a checked observation gives it current standing, once-only grants included. Reserve that place synchronously after the await so concurrent arrivals cannot pass 4,096.\n3. Keys already admitted keep run-sticky denial for the whole run, as authority.ts:25-30 and held() require today.\n4. Revoked keys that were never admitted go in a separate bounded FIFO. When an entry leaves the FIFO, invalidate the standing handles created before that eviction. A cache miss then reads Membership again.\n\nThe changed guarantee is acceptable. Membership never reverses a retirement or a removal, so a fresh trusted read refuses the key again. The run cache remains a performance and ordering guard, and Membership stays the source of truth. A caller can push entries out of the FIFO only with distinct revoked keys, and only real revocations create those.\n\nWitnesses: the newcomer witness and its control, as 31f98f33 states. Add one witness for the eviction path: after a revoked, never-admitted key leaves the FIFO, an older in-flight active answer for that key does not admit it. Pair it with one control that removes the invalidation and makes that witness fail.\n\nDocs: the threat-model residual paragraph states the FIFO size, the changed guarantee for never-admitted keys, and that `limit` now needs 4,096 keys with standing in one run.\n\nSlot order: BR14's diagnostic and gate come first, then R3a's gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}